{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fixed in change 3370, merged as 2102dcfb220 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1; make verify rc=0: 21,162 + 218 passed). Root cause: the slow_ls_tree fixture shrank git_fetch._GIT_TIMEOUT to 1 s for the whole test, so the recovery materialize (real ls-tree, hang switched off) also had a 1 s budget. The fixture now applies the 1 s bound only while the hang is on and restores the production bound when it is switched off. New test test_recovery_listing_is_not_bound_by_the_slow_path_budget injects an ls-tree that answers after 2 s on the recovery call (a loaded host): FAILED before, passes now. AC2: the module passed 5 of 5 runs under 16 bounded CPU burners at load average 66 (burners reaped)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794491145715609792,"uuid":"07c4119b-1d64-4ffd-87db-6078a1d37db8"}